-- title:
--   Geometric characteristic-p fibres of the model are not smooth
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $p$ that is prime, a nonzero level $M$ with $p \mid M$, and a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$; let $hj$ record that the Laurent series $j(q)$ (`jqModC ℚ`, namely $q^{-1}$ times the integral power series `jNum` pushed to $\mathbb{Q}$) lies in `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`, the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the ratios `intFormRatiosC` for the full modular group $SL(2,\mathbb{Z})$. Let $\mathfrak{X}$ be an inhabitant of the structure `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`, which bundles, for the two-chart integral model `X p (ΓM M H) hj` of the function field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (ΓM M H)` over the base ring `R p` with its structure morphism `toBase` (obtained from the charts generated by `jAt` and its inverse), the assertions that `toBase` is proper, flat and locally of finite presentation with integral and normal source, that the corresponding model at level `ΓN p M H hpM` is proper and smooth of relative dimension one, a curve model over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with function field `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` identified with the base change of $\mathfrak X$ together with its Galois equivariance and $q$-expansion normalisation, and smoothness of relative dimension one plus geometric integrality of the generic fibre. The conclusion is that for every algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $p$ and every morphism $x : \operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{R}\ p)$, the second projection of the fibre product of `toBase p (ΓM M H) hj` with $x$, that is the base-changed morphism $\mathfrak{X}_k \to \operatorname{Spec} k$, is not smooth.
--
--   This is the bad-reduction statement for $X_H(M)$ at a prime $p$ dividing the level: the geometric fibre in characteristic $p$ of the Deligne–Rapoport model is singular, classically because it is a union of two copies of a curve of level $M/p$ crossing at the supersingular points. It is used in the analysis of the special fibre and of components of the base change, being cited by [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.fibre_w_mem_diff_connectedComponentIn_and_cuspZero_mem_baseChange`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.fibre_w_mem_diff_connectedComponentIn_and_cuspZero_mem_baseChange) and by [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.nonempty_iso_unit_of_isAlgEquivZero_of_ne_zero_fibre`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.nonempty_iso_unit_of_isAlgEquivZero_of_ne_zero_fibre).
